{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iyilang/iyi/pulls/147","id":5001441126,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTsez1M8AAAABKhvvZg","html_url":"https://github.com/iyilang/iyi/pull/147","diff_url":"https://github.com/iyilang/iyi/pull/147.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/iyilang/iyi/pull/147.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iyilang/iyi/issues/147","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iyilang/iyi/pulls/147/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iyilang/iyi/pulls/147/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iyilang/iyi/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iyilang/iyi/issues/147/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iyilang/iyi/statuses/180f14f91c829b25362a5ed34b20847f3ac2db77","number":147,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"iyi test --cached: native stale testing (opt-in)","user":{"login":"jwaldrip","id":43164,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzMTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43164?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwaldrip","html_url":"https://github.com/jwaldrip","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwaldrip/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwaldrip/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwaldrip/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwaldrip/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwaldrip/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwaldrip/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwaldrip/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwaldrip/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwaldrip/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Native stale testing for `iyi test`, built to the plan in `STALE_TESTS_DESIGN.md`. Default `iyi test` is unchanged; `--cached` is opt-in.\n\n## What it does\n\n`iyi test --cached` serves a passing verdict from a receipt when the test's build key is equal (toolchain, behavior, compiler environment, link, and `CallPathFp` over the reached, typed call path) and every observation the recording run made replays equal now. Nothing past semantic analysis runs on a hit. `--fresh` reruns and records under `-Diyi_observe`, `--explain` names why a test ran, and `--json` adds `cached`, `source`, `reuse` and `reason`. A test that reads the clock, entropy, network, processes, signals and the like, uses an opaque construct, or writes outside its scratch directory is not reusable and runs every time.\n\n## Verification status\n\n- Prior product candidate `834ed99a819c65cb2c2f22e1f8912eea44cfa16d`: full fork CI passed on run 42208304066 attempt 3 (all checks green, release intentionally skipped; stale acceptance and fresh receipt audit passed; Windows shards passed).\n- Current merge candidate `180f14f91c829b25362a5ed34b20847f3ac2db77`: rebased and merged cleanly with upstream master (incorporating definition witnesses #118 and Windows test scheduling #157); hosted PR checks are currently pending.\n- Full strict backtrace equivalence (141 final) remains unproven. It is not claimed, and merge readiness is not implied. This PR remains a draft while proof is pending.\n\n## Proof (macOS arm64, baseline at 110ee7b47)\n\n- Full local gate green: format, compiler specs (14,616 examples, 0 failures), primitives (716), samples, round trip, dependency and identity floors, panics, `doc_numbers.py`.\n- `bench/stale_tests.sh`: section 12 rows 1-22 and 25-50 automated and green. Rows 23-24 are CI-only.\n- RG1 and RG7 (`stale_reproducible.sh`), RG2 141 of 141 and RG5 20 of 20 (`stale_equivalence.sh`), RG3 0 unclassified sites, RG4, RG8 over 7 programs, RG9 over 141. RG6 is wired in CI and provable only on master.\n- End to end: a body edit to an unreached def hits both tests; an edit to a reached def reruns only the test that reaches it, and `--explain` names `lib/util.iyi`; default output is unchanged.\n\n## Measured, not claimed\n\n- Census over 141 programs: 90 reusable on a second run (C2 24 of 27, C3 66 of 114), 138 by static build key, 0 build failures, 0 internal reasons.\n- A `--cached` hit took 1.03 to 1.13 s, slower than a warm default build and run (0.50 to 0.85 s) for every measured program but one. No speedup is claimed.\n\n## Found and fixed during the build\n\n- A test's writes in its own scratch directory were read as shared writes: the runtime lost the scratch path before the program ran (row 49).\n- A variable a test set and read back missed every run (row 6).\n- The compiler-environment key differed between cold and warm builds of a program with a macro `run` helper (row 50).\n- Four exercises that failed under load or on this machine's network stack (dns, digest, big, tar), and a compiler `Regex` that pulled pcre2 past the dependency floor.\n\n## Not done\n\nCompletion per design section 13 is not met and the default stays off: rows 23-24, RG6, and master consumption and audit need CI on master, and the census still has 5 runner reasons (tests that write beside themselves). Full strict backtrace equivalence (141 final) is unproven.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T03:21:28Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T13:11:15Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"ce6da945a7f54e15a12787673e3ebed6ada1ed1d","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"jwaldrip:plan/native-stale-testing","ref":"plan/native-stale-testing","repo":{"id":1340355933,"node_id":"R_kgDOT-Q1XQ","name":"iyi","full_name":"jwaldrip/iyi","owner":{"login":"jwaldrip","id":43164,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzMTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43164?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwaldrip","html_url":"https://github.com/jwaldrip","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwaldrip/followers","following_